    "_meanings": [
        ".²1 A quality (good or bad); {#suguRa, durguRa#}; {#yadaNganArUpasarUpatAyAH#}\n {#kaYcidguRaM BedakamicCatIBiH#} <ls>Śi. 3. 42</ls>.\n",
        ".²2\n",
        ".³({%a%}) A good quality, merit, virtue, excellence; {#katame te guRAH#}\n <ls>Māl. 1</ls>; {#vasanti hi premRi guRA na vastuni#} <ls>Ki. 8. 37</ls>; <ls>R. 1. 9</ls>, <ls n=\"R. 1.\">22</ls>;\n {#sADutve tasya ko guRaH#} <ls>Pt. 4. 108</ls>.\n",
        ".³({%b%}) Eminence.\n",
        ".²3 Use, advantage, good (with <ab>instr.</ab> usually), <ls>Pt. 5</ls>; {#kaH sTAnalABe#}\n {#guRaH#} <ls n=\"Pt.\">2. 21</ls>; <ls>H. 1. 49</ls>; <ls>Mu. 1. 15</ls>.\n",
        ".²4 Effect, result, efficacy, good result; {#saMBAvanAguRamavehi tamISvarARAm#}\n <ls>Ś. 7. 4</ls>; {#guRamahatAM mahate guRAya yogaH#} <ls>Ki. 10. 25</ls>, <ls n=\"Ki.\">6. 7</ls>.\n",
        ".²5\n",
        ".³({%a%}) A single thread or string.\n",
        ".³({%b%}) Thread, string, rope, cord, {#meKalAguREH#} <ls>Ku. 4. 8</ls>, <ls n=\"Ku.\">5. 10</ls>;\n {#tfRErguRatvamApannErbaDyante mattadantinaH#} <ls>H. 1. 32</ls>; {#yataH parezAM#}\n {#guRagrahItAsi#} <ls>Bv. 1. 9</ls> (where {#guRa#} also means ‘a merit’).\n",
        ".²6 The bow-string; {#guRakftye Danuzo niyojitA#} <ls>Ku. 4. 15</ls>, <ls n=\"Ku. 4.\">29</ls>; {#kanakapiNgataqidguRasaMyutam#} <ls>R. 9. 54</ls>.\n",
        ".²7 The string of a musical instrument; {#kalavallakIguRasvAnamAnam#} <ls>Śi. 4. 57</ls>.\n",
        ".²8 A sinew.\n",
        ".²9 A quality, attribute, property in general; {#yAdfgguRena BartrA strI#}\n {#saMyujyeta yaTAviDi#} <ls>Ms. 9. 22</ls>.\n",
        ".²10 A quality, characteristic or property of all substances, one of the\n seven categories of {%padārthas%} of the Vaiśeṣikas, (the number of\n these properties is 24).\n",
        ".²11 An ingredient or constituent of nature, any one of the three properties\n belonging to all created things; (these are {#sattva, rajas#} and {#tamas#});\n {#guRatrayaviBAgAya#} <ls>Ku. 2. 4</ls>; {#sattvaM rajastama iti guRAH prakftisaMBavAH#}\n <ls>Bg. 14. 5</ls>; <ls>R. 3. 27</ls>.\n",
        ".²12 A wick, cotton thread; {#nfpadIpo DanasnehaM prajAByaH saMharannapi .#}\n {#antarasTErguREH SuBrErlakzyate nEva kenacit ..#} <ls>Pt. 1. 221</ls>.\n",
        ".²13 An object of sense, (these are five {#rUpa, rasa, ganDa, sparSa#},\n and {#Sabda#}); {#guRErguRAnsa BuYjAna AtmapradyotitEH praBuH#} <ls>Bhāg. 11. 3. 5</ls>.\n",
        ".²14 Repetition, multiplication, denoting ‘folds’ or ‘times’, usually at\n the end of <ab>comp.</ab> after numerals; {#AhAro dviguRaH strIRAM budDistAsAM#}\n {#caturguRA . zaqguRo vyavasAyaSca kAmaScAzwaguRaH smftaH ..#} <ls>Chāṇ. 78</ls>;\n so {#triguRa#}; {#SataguRIBavati#} becomes a hundred-fold, {#aDyarDaguRamAhuryaM#}\n {#bale SOrye ca keSava#} <ls>Mb. 11. 20. 1</ls>.\n",
        ".²15 A secondary element, a subordinate part (<ab>opp.</ab> {#muKya#}); {#na ca#}\n {#guRAnugrahArTaM praDAnasyAvfttiryuktA#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 4</ls>.\n",
        ".²16 Excess, abundance, superfluity; {#parANmuKavaDaM kftvA ko'tra prAptastvayA#}\n {#guRaH#} <ls>Rām. 4. 17. 16</ls>.\n",
        ".²17 An adjective, a word subordinate to another in a sentence.\n",
        ".²18 The substitution of {#e, o, ar#} and {#al#} for {#i, u, f#} (short\n or long) and {#x#}, or the vowels {#a, e, o#} and {#ar#} and {#al#}.\n",
        ".²19 (In <ab>Rhet.</ab>) Quality considered as an inherent property of a {%Rasa%}\n or sentiment. Mammaṭa thus defines {#guRa#}.{#--ye rahasyANgino DarmAH#}\n {#SOryAdaya ivAtmanaH . utkarzahetavaste syuracalasTitayo guRAH ..#} <ls>K. P. 8</ls>.\n (Some writers on rhetoric, such as Vāmana, Jagannātha Paṇḍita,\n Daṇḍin and others, consider {%Guṇas%} to be properties both of {#Sabda#}\n and {#arTa#}, and mention ten varieties under each head. Mammaṭa, however,\n recognises only three, and, after discussing and criticizing the views\n of others, says: {#mADuryEjaHprasAdAKyAstrayaste na punardaSa#} <ls>K. P. 8</ls>); <ls>Ki. 17. 6</ls>.\n\n\n",
        ".²20 (In <ab>gram.</ab> and <ab>Mīm.</ab>) Property considered as the meaning of a class\n of words; {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} grammarians recognise four kinds of the meaning of\n words; {#jAti, guRa, kriyA#} and {#dravya#}, and give {#gOH, SuklaH, calaH#}\n and {#qitTaH#} as instances to illustrate these meanings.\n",
        ".²21 (In politics) A proper course of action, an expedient. (The expedients\n to be used by a king in foreign politics are six:-- 1 {#sanDi#} peace\n or alliance; 2 {#vigraha#} war; 3 {#yAna#} march or expedition; 4 {#sTAna#}\n or {#Asana#} halt; 5 {#saMSraya#} seeking shelter; 6 {#dvEDa#} or {#dvEDIBAva#}\n duplicity; {#sanDirnA vigraho yAnamAsanaM dvEDamASrayaH#} <ls>Ak.</ls>) see <ls>Y. 1. 346</ls>; <ls>Ms. 7. 160</ls>;\n <ls>Śi. 2. 26</ls>; <ls>R. 8. 21</ls>.\n",
        ".²22 The number ‘three’ (derived from the three qualities).\n",
        ".²23 The chord of an arc (in <ab>geom.</ab>).\n",
        ".²24 An organ of sense.\n",
        ".²25 A subordinate dish; <ls>Ms. 3. 226</ls>, <ls n=\"Ms. 3.\">233</ls>.\n",
        ".²26 A cook.\n",
        ".²27 An epithet of Bhīma as in {#yuDizWiro'pi guRapriyaH#} <ls>Vās.</ls>\n",
        ".²28 Leaving, abandonment.\n",
        ".²29 A multiplier, coefficient (in <ab>math.</ab>)\n",
        ".²30 Division, subdivision, species, kind.\n",
        ".²31 The peculiar property of letters which are pronounced with external\n utterance ({#bAhyaprayatna#}); they are eleven.\n"
